user_impact:
Whoever controls the content at a feed URL the site previews or syncs can pin a PHP worker for minutes and use hundreds of MB to over 1 GB. That can be a compromised or malicious podcast host, or a feed linked from a web page an admin pastes into the import. In mirror mode it repeats every hour from WP-Cron. Because the fatal error happens before any state is written:
- the failure is never counted, so there is no back-off and no admin notice;
- the import lock blocks 'Sync now' and imports for 5 minutes ('An import is running');
- the next run hits the same feed again.
Previews write job files of tens of MB into uploads.

